# Pulsar Pause — scripted mid-print pause for inserts / inspection.
#
# pulsar_pause() clears global.pulsar_running, so the daemon stops
# feeding chunks and the screw halts within ~one chunk (~0.3-0.8 s). No
# retract — on a screw extruder a few mm of E-retract is swallowed by the
# melt volume; stopping the screw is what breaks the bead. The popup
# blocks (operator does the insert); pulsar_resume() restarts the screw
# at the current rate when they click OK.

pulsar_pause()

popup("Insert hardware now. Click OK to resume.", title="Pause", warning=False, error=False, blocking=True)

pulsar_resume()
